  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-099-0002</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe Motherhood in Koussan&#xe9; - Mission Sisters</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to health care is a luxury in the commune of Koussane and SMK project provides some assistance to these populations. It will be a question of continuing this assistance by adding a component to fight against chronic malnutrition. This assistance will be based on improved and locally produced flour as well as awareness sessions and cooking demonstrations  performed by volunteers and the project team.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commune of Koussan&#xe9; (Kayes Region)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">First step is to maintain the team working in the current Safe Motherhoods Koussane (SMK) project, to rely on their work and experience as well as knowledge of the environment to initiate this shift and provide assistance to populations in need. The 28 villages of the Commune of Koussane are in extreme  poverty with a flagrant delay in terms of investment and a lack of basic social services. Needs are such that it is absolutely necessary to prioritize this commune for interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Koussan&#xe9;, Kayes region, Mali</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross in partnership with the Malian Red Cross have set up a project to support access to health care for pregnant women and children under 59 months of age called: Maternal and Child Health Care in Kayes (Safe Motherhoods Koussan&#xe9;, funded by the Disaster Response Unit). This proposal aims to continue and leverage on the most essential actions that are currently taking place under the Safe Motherhood Project in Koussan&#xe9; funded by the DRU.</narrative>
  </description>
